Test the specified :00 momentum strategy: it works, momentum does not

Implemented exactly as written - close from the ticker, side frozen at entry,
first complete quote at 8-14 min, exactly two minutes of wait. The derived
`won` was verified against underlying.parquet at 1.000000 agreement on 1,878
markets before any result was computed.

SPEC AS WRITTEN

  161 trades / 66 days   win 87.58%   mean ask 78.60c
  +$188.66 at q15, fees $28.09
  +7.81c per contract   95% CI [+2.61, +12.65]   P(<=0) 0.0021
  train +9.53c / valid +5.60c / test +7.31c - positive in all three
  leave-one-coin-out and leave-one-week-out all positive
  dropping the best 5 trades still leaves +7.15c

Permutation over the ENTIRE search - shuffle outcomes within day, re-run every
configuration, take the best each time - gives a permuted best of -1.38c
(p95 +1.60c) against the observed +7.81c: P = 0.0000. This is not a search
artifact. Bonferroni over ~20 variants also passes, though only just
(0.0021 < 0.0025).

BUT THREE OF THE FOUR DELAYED CONDITIONS ARE INERT

Removing one condition at a time and keeping the rest:

  full spec                161  +7.81c  $2.86/day
  - momentum (rise >= 2c)  182  +8.52c  $3.37/day   BETTER without it
  - volume (>= 2000)       325  +7.75c  $5.17/day   same edge, 2x frequency
  - spread widen (<= 1c)   181  +8.10c  $3.23/day   no effect
  - ask ceiling            203  +5.54c  $2.44/day   this one is real

The momentum filter is the headline idea and it is doing nothing - removing it
improves the edge on more trades. Volume costs $2.31/day for an identical
edge. Only the ask ceiling earns its place.

THE 2-MINUTE WAIT IS A NOISE PEAK

  wait 1  +2.10c   wait 2  +7.81c   wait 3  +1.08c   wait 4  +2.20c

A sharp peak at exactly the specified value is a warning sign, so it was
tested directly: wait-2 minus wait-1, day-paired on 62 shared days, is +3.13c
with 95% CI [-2.94, +9.72], P(<=0) 0.1664. Not significant. The choice of two
minutes should not be treated as load-bearing.

HIGHEST-EARNING CONFIGURATION - drop volume and momentum:

  362 trades  win 87.02%  +7.52c/contract  $5.59/day at q15
  95% CI [+4.13, +10.84]  P(<=0) 0.0000, all leave-one-outs positive

WARNING - CHRONOLOGICAL DECAY in that configuration:

  train n=160 win 0.9062 +11.26c
  valid n=105 win 0.8667  +6.48c
  test  n= 97 win 0.8144  +2.47c

Monotone decline, 9 points of win rate from train to test. Either the effect
is being priced away or n~100 per split is simply small; this data cannot
separate them. The full spec does not show the same pattern, which argues for
noise, but the magnitude should be planned around the TEST figure (+2.47c,
~$1.80/day) rather than the full-sample one.

Also noted: mean ask 78.60c means a loss costs 3.7x what a win pays, so the
87% win rate is carrying everything and is expensive to lose.

139 tests still pass.

